            <ArticleTitle>Thalamic syndrome caused by unruptured cerebral aneurysm. Case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>291-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case is reported of a 63-year-old woman with thalamic syndrome as the presenting feature of an unruptured cerebral aneurysm. Unruptured aneurysm is a rare cause of thalamic syndrome; the possible mechanisms of production of the sensory disturbance are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
